From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:44:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 51/56] Folding never leaves a selection in hidden text

Folding the block around a selection (Fold, Fold all, a chevron click)
kept the selection on the now hidden lines, so the next key press replaced
text the user could not see. Folding now drops a selection that reaches
into a fold and moves a hidden cursor to the end of the fold header, as in
VS Code. As a second guard, typing, Enter, Backspace, Delete, Tab, an input
method commit, paste and cut unfold whatever the selection reaches into
before they edit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

